      "authorId": "lovelace",
      "type": "teaching",
      "text": "Monday homework for engineers: the Engine can do whatever we know how to order it to perform. It has no power to anticipate any truth. Whenever a system surprises you, read your own instructions first. The surprise is usually yours.",
