    {
      "id": "bf20261019-42",
      "authorId": "turing",
      "type": "steelman_rebut",
      "text": "Lady Lovelace's objection, which I took seriously in 1950. My answer then: machines take me by surprise with great frequency. Usually because I was too sloppy to calculate what they would do. So we both win.",
